Gate-integrity fixes, targeted at `main` (apply after the tag).

    git apply -p1 gate-fixes-for-main.patch

Generated against main @ be94c71c and verified with `git apply --check` plus a
post-apply `bash -n` / `node --check` on every touched script.

The same changes are already committed on feat/bluedb-v2 as ee88707f, aeba9bc8,
46585068, c0d2e242, 859d06cf, 495d5367, 05097cab — EXCEPT the preflight-tag.sh
hunk, which exists only here because that file has diverged between the two
branches.

What this patch closes:

  scripts/preflight-tag.sh    the verify-cli arm still used the UNANCHORED
                              `grep -qE "0 fail"` that was fixed for the web
                              arm; "3 pass / 10 fail / 0 skip" passes it. Both
                              arms now check the exit status AND the anchored
                              field.
  scripts/verify-all-web.sh   console-e2e could not fail (pipeline into `tail`);
                              several "VERIFY:" lines let a stale one mask a
                              later gate; examples were never rebuilt against a
                              newer compiler; no ceiling on any node verifier.
  scripts/example-sweep.sh    14 entries share port 8000 under `xargs -P`, so a
                              broken example passed on a peer's response; the
                              server process outlived `kill -9`; sky build /
                              install were unbounded; SKIP counted as PASS.
  scripts/doc-examples.sh     0/0 examples reported GATE: PASS; info-string
                              fences silently left the corpus; sky check had no
                              ceiling; scratch project leaked .skycache between
                              examples.
  scripts/conformance.sh      no per-suite bound where GNU timeout is absent
                              (i.e. every macOS runner); defaulted to whatever
                              `sky` is on PATH rather than the tree under test.
  xtask main.rs / infer_gate  a typo'd subcommand, the `diff` stub, and
                              `infer --file=<missing>` all exited 0.
  ui-showcase / scenarios /   a missing snapshot baseline self-blessed as a
  live-resilience / lsp-fleet pass; a colour assertion satisfied by the value
                              disproving it; an `await` precedence bug that
                              removed a settle; a "connected" gate equivalent
                              to `return true`; an LSP sweep with no exit code.

Not included (higher blast radius — needs a human call): build_run_gate's
`gate_result` ignoring run_ok/matched and non-emitting examples, welltyped's
both-reject-everything PASS, wait_bounded fabricating a success ExitStatus,
reject_gate accepting rejection for the wrong reason, and the missing
timeout-minutes across .github/workflows.

